cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Drift: a memory link between frozen language models"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: ashhart
    alias: ashhart
repository-code: "https://github.com/ashhart/Drift"
abstract: >-
  Drift connects frozen language models through their key-value caches.
  Model-specific taps capture working memory, trained translators map it into a
  form the receiving model can attend to, and the receiver reads it alongside
  its own context. Backbone weights stay frozen and the designated activation
  channel carries no task text or token IDs. This is experimental research
  code; published results are bounded engineering qualifications rather than
  general recall guarantees.
keywords:
  - key-value cache
  - model-to-model communication
  - agent workflows
  - RDMA
  - frozen models
license: Apache-2.0
